                                "example_id": "91a7b900-1ffd-4a96-a693-cee8d43b33a7",
                                "sense_id": "71815db5-e7b5-348b-a137-949aa77189d9",
                                "text": "The line from Nyon to La Cure (17½ miles) was opened in 1916, and is on independent track throughout, leaving the road immediately after passing under the Swiss Federal line from Lausanne to Geneva, where grooved tramrails with tie-bars give place to steel-sleepered track."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "da4f1412-0cf1-47bc-aba0-e5d1cb049862",
                                "sense_id": "71815db5-e7b5-348b-a137-949aa77189d9",
                                "text": "Nor, having married coach and bogie design successfully, does it follow that good riding will ensue, whatever the track carrying it—as the performance of B.R. standard coaches on flat-bottom, concrete-sleepered track bears witness."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
